From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 03:55:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] book ch.9: latin square, split-plot and BIBD analyses

- latin_square_anova: Row, Column and Row.Column strata; single treatment
  factor or crossed A*B with marginality-based prediction tables.
- split_plot_anova: Block, Block.WholePlot and subplot strata (whole plots
  from a column or block x A), F tests against stratum residuals, prediction
  SEs/SEDs per stratum with Satterthwaite df for cross-stratum comparisons;
  also the unblocked variant.
- bibd_anova: design check (t, n, m, u, lambda, EF), between-block treatment
  SS in the block stratum, intra-block adjusted means and SED = sqrt(2s2/(nEF)),
  inter-block effects.
- SS from nested least-squares fits (rank-based df); catalog, bridge, i18n.
- Tests against Tables 9.2, 9.4-9.6, 9.12, 9.14, Example 9.5C, 9.9B and OLS.

